  "source_interpretation": [
    "GAO p3 explicitly describes no settlement and actual submission of recommendations to District Court on1975-12-12. Its section4-type report is an occurrence fact, distinct from later1979 partition. It is retrospective official factual evidence, not an operative legal instrument.",
    "Statute section1(a) supplies alternative cessation upon entered full agreement or report submission after negotiation default/partial agreement. Sections2-4 explain failed-negotiation route and90-day deadline; deadline alone is insufficient.",
    "EO11829 section4 imports that actual statutory cessation condition. It does not make notice a prerequisite to Committee dissolution, and separately commands transfer of any maintained records.",
    "EO11853 changes only parent section2(a), continues amended per owner ruling, leaves the parent notice/records commands intact but does not make them duties of the amending instrument.",
    "Relocation Commission is a separate section12 statutory body, with different composition, support and presidential-determination sunset; continuing relocation activity does not sustain the Interagency Committee.",
    "EO12379 directly names EO11829 as amended on1982-08-17, no deferred date or target savings in full text. It neither directly names EO11853 nor proves earlier performance or first cessation."
  ],
